#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# accuracy

#% text
# `accuracy(x)` gives the number of correct decimal digits after the decimal point of `x`, `-log10` of its error bound.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Exact numbers have accuracy `inf`; for an expression it is the least accuracy of its numbers.

#% item
# Accuracy and precision differ by the size of the number: `precision(x)` is about `accuracy(x) + log10(abs(x))`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
accuracy(1/3)
#% output
#= inf

#% cell
accuracy(1~20)
#% output
#= 20.16900970948674

#% cell
accuracy(1000~20)
#% output
#= 17.169009709486744

#% cell
accuracy(0.001~20)
#% output
#= 23.169009709486737

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# Precision and accuracy of the same ball:

#% cell
x = 12345.678~20; [precision(x), accuracy(x)]
#% output
#= [20.16900970948674, 16.07749476397754]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `precision`, `set_precision`, `n`
